# TypeScript Conventions

## Types in Dedicated Files
All types, interfaces, enums, and DTOs live in `src/types/` — never inline in component files.

```
src/types/
  product.ts     # Product, ProductCard, ProductFilters, Category
  order.ts       # Order, OrderItem, OrderStatus, ShippingAddress
  user.ts        # UserProfile, UserRole, GuestUser
  review.ts      # Review, ReviewForm, ReviewFilters
  cart.ts        # CartItem, CartState
  payment.ts     # CashfreeOrder, PaymentStatus
  api.ts         # ApiResponse<T>, PaginatedResponse<T>
  common.ts      # Pagination, SortOrder, DateRange
```

## Naming Conventions
- Interfaces: `PascalCase` (e.g. `ProductCard`, `OrderItem`)
- Enums: `PascalCase` with `SCREAMING_SNAKE_CASE` values (e.g. `OrderStatus.PENDING`)
- Type aliases: `PascalCase` (e.g. `UserRole = 'user' | 'admin'`)
- Generic wrappers: `ApiResponse<T>`, `PaginatedResponse<T>`

## Strict Rules
- Never use `any` — use `unknown` and narrow with type guards.
- Always type function parameters and return values.
- Use `Readonly<T>` for props that should not be mutated.

```ts
// ❌ BAD
const handler = (data: any) => { ... }

// ✅ GOOD
const handler = (data: ApiResponse<Product>): void => { ... }
```

## Component Props
- Define props as a named interface in the component file ONLY if < 5 props and not reused.
- If reused across components, move to `src/types/`.

```tsx
// Props used only in this component — OK inline
interface Props {
  title: string;
  isActive: boolean;
}

// Reused props — must go in src/types/product.ts
export interface ProductCardProps {
  product: Product;
  onAddToCart: (id: string) => void;
}
```
